 Notes on Your FarmGrid CSS (Mobile-First Responsive Design)

 1. What the stylesheet does
It styles a farm website with a header and navigation, a hero banner, an intro section, three service cards and a footer. It is **mobile-first**: the base styles are for phones, and media queries add layouts for tablets and desktops.

## 2. Problems in the pasted code

1. **Missing `/* */` on most comments.** Headings like `FARMGRID - GLOBAL STYLES`, `HEADER`, `NAVIGATION` and `Service Cards` are plain text, so the browser treats them as broken CSS and may ignore the rules after them. Only the `SERVICES` and `FOOTER` comments are correct.
2. **Missing `*` selector.** The first rule starts with `{ margin: 0; ... }` and has no selector. It should be `* { ... }`.
3. **Stray `css` at the top and ` ``` ` at the bottom.** These are Markdown leftovers and must be removed from `style.css`.
4. **Image path.** `url("images/farm.jpg")` only works if an `images` folder is in the same folder as the CSS file.

Fix pattern:

```css
/* =========================
   FARMGRID - GLOBAL STYLES
   ========================= */
* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* Service Cards */
.service-box { ... }

/* =========================
   RESPONSIVE DESIGN
   Tablet / Desktop
   ========================= */
@media (min-width: 768px) { ... }
```

## 3. Key CSS concepts used

| Concept | Where | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Universal selector `*` | global reset | Removes default margins and padding |
| `box-sizing: border-box` | global reset | Padding and border count inside the element's width |
| Element, class and pseudo-class selectors | `nav a:hover`, `.hero` | Target elements and states |
| Flexbox | `nav`, `.hero`, `.services` | One-dimensional layout (row or column) |
| CSS Grid | `.services` at 768px+ | Two-dimensional layout (3 equal columns) |
| `grid-column: 1 / -1` | `.services h2` | Makes the heading span all columns |
| `linear-gradient` over `url()` | `.hero` | Dark overlay on the background image |
| `background-size: cover` | `.hero` | Image fills the whole area |
| `vh` and `rem` units | hero, fonts | Relative to the viewport and root font size |
| `transition` and `transform` | buttons, cards | Smooth hover animation |
| `box-shadow`, `border-radius` | `.service-box` | Depth and rounded corners |
| Media queries | 768px, 1200px | Change layout by screen width |
| `max-width: 100%; height: auto` | `img` | Responsive images |
| `:focus` and `outline` | links, inputs | Keyboard accessibility |

 4. Mobile-first breakpoints

| Screen | Layout |
|---|---|
| Below 768px (phone) | Header and nav stacked; services in one column |
| 768px and above (tablet/desktop) | Header and nav in a row; services in a 3-column grid; larger hero text |
| 1200px and above (large screens) | Hero text larger; wider side padding on services |

 5. Colour scheme

| Colour | Use |
|---|---|
| `#1b5e20` (dark green) | Header, headings |
| `#2e7d32` / `#388e3c` | Card headings, nav hover |
| `#ffb300` (amber) | Hero button, focus outline |
| `#f4f8f1` / `#e8f5e9` | Page and section backgrounds |
| `#123b16` | Footer |

## 6. Matching HTML structure

```html
<header>
  <h1>FarmGrid</h1>
  <nav><a href="#">Home</a> <a href="#">Services</a> <a href="#">Contact</a></nav>
</header>
<main>
  <section class="hero"><h2>...</h2><p>...</p><a href="#">Get Started</a></section>
  <section class="intro"><h2>...</h2><p>...</p></section>
  <section class="services">
    <h2>Our Services</h2>
    <div class="service-box"><h3>...</h3><p>...</p></div>
    <!-- two more service boxes -->
  </section>
</main>
<footer>...</footer>
```

Remember `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">` in the `<head>`. Without it, media queries will not work properly on phones.

## 7. Possible improvements
- Use CSS variables (`--green: #1b5e20;`) so colours are defined once.
- Add `scroll-behavior: smooth;` for smooth in-page navigation.
- Add a `:focus-visible` rule instead of `:focus` so the outline shows only for keyboard users.
- Add a `prefers-reduced-motion` media query to turn off animations for users who need it.
- Make the header `position: sticky`.

## 8. Points for an exam or report
- **Mobile-first approach:** base styles for small screens, `min-width` queries for larger ones.
- **Flexbox vs Grid:** Flexbox for one-direction layouts, Grid for rows and columns together.
- **Accessibility:** visible focus outlines, good colour contrast, responsive images.
- **Separation of concerns:** HTML for structure, CSS for presentation.
- **Maintainability:** organised sections with clear comments.

